.TH ULID "1" "February 2024" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
.B ulid
\(en Create or inspect ULIDs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ulid
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB { build , show }\ ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
A ULID is a universally unique
lexicographically sortable identifier
with the following structure
.P
.in +7n
.EX
\ 01AN4Z07BY\ \ \ \ \ \ 79KA1307SR9X4MV3
|\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|\ \ \ \ |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
\ Timestamp\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ Randomness
\ \ \ 48bits\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 80bits 
.EE
.in
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "OPTIONAL\ ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.B \-h\fR,\ \fB\-\-help
show a help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version\fR,\ \fB\-V
show program\(cqs version number and exit
.SS "SUBCOMMANDS"
.RB { build , show }
.TP
.B build
generate ULIDs from different sources
.IP
See
.BR ulid\-build (1).
.TP
.B show
show properties of a ULID
.IP
See
.BR ulid\-show (1).
.SH "SEE\ ALSO"
.BR ulid\-build (1),
.BR ulid\-show (1)
